      "side": 1,
      "message": "That was my first thought too but after all IMHO current version is better.\nRationale for that is `HandleStartSyncRequest` is a place only to StartSyncRequest without any internal logic of the PeriodicSyncManager.  Notice that it even get data as arguments from `pending_sync_requests_`. There could be return, but only if that StartSyncRequest cannot execute because of some external thing like `EnqueueCommand` fail. `HandleNextRequest` is a place with actual logic of the PeriodicSyncManager, here if conditions are ok (pending_sync_requests_ and periodic_syncs_ are ok) and StartSyncRequest is success (always success) we change our internal state of the periodic_syncs_ and start the timer (which always was there and there is no difference with it and with this `sync-\u003esync_state \u003d PERIODIC_SYNC_STATE_PENDING;` in logic context.",
